/Title (The Technology Innovation and Entrepreneurship Center \(TIEC\) is an initiative of our institute dedicated to identifying entrepreneurial traits in students, nurturing technical capacity, and supporting campus technology startups. Functioning as a business incubator, TIEC serves as a commercial extension of campus research, enabling the conversion of innovations into market-ready products that address real world industry and societal needs. By championing a sustainable small-town business model, the center bridges regional employment gaps and counters tier-1 city migration offering corporations a cost effective, high yield alternative to metropolitan operational challenges.)
